pecting love you actually hit  them know what I put forward was the  problems that people face in this  country and why I disagree with the  political philosophy being pursued by  the government and obviously by the  Conservative Party on the kind of  society they want to create in Britain  and what I think would be much better  which is a society where we recognize  the huge abilities and talents of  everybody particularly the poorest  people who are often locked out of the  possibility of achieving anything by low  wages by bad housing by insufficient  educational opportunities I want to  unlock the talent of everybody that is  the philosophy I was putting forward I  know  I know and you see all that signs  brilliant but if I was running a company  or you get chief executives listening  basically you're running a company  they're going to say look it's nice to  take into account what people have to  say but the way you put this across  everybody joined the party will listen  to all of you if you did really do that  you'd be too busy listening to ever do  anything so what it gonna happen is it  there is a democratic open process  within the Labor Party and all the  affiliates the Labour Party there is  huge talent all through that membership  we've got nearly four hundred thousand  members and growing very very fast but  at the mall in having their vote they're  interested in having their voice heard  they don't want the idea that there's be  some all-seeing all-knowing leader that  will decide everything yes at the end of  the day a policy decision will come  we'll come to that and we'll make an  agreement on aspects of housing policy  aspects of economic policy gear all  those things but surely at the start of  this process you set out what your  general philosophy is you set out how  you're going to be inclusive to all  people surely that's something that's  good about politics good about a  democratic society if it works and it's  like running a government doesn't like  to talk to you find time to see if it  but actually does work but you know it's  one thing listening to the party what if  you've got a disunited  party not even a disunited party at this  united cabinet because Parliament may  soon be asked to take a big decision on  further action in Syria are you happy to  lead a disunited party on that matter  from Hillary ban to Diane Abbott look I  was elected with over 250,000 votes of  party members and supporters I have a  huge mandate 60 percent of those that  voted voted for me to be the leader yes  there are people in the parliamentary  Labour Party who have a different  approach to the situation in Syria I  fully understand that there is a  possibility that the UN discussions  going on between President Putin and  President Obama and others will lead  some way towards a political solution  that's a good thing let's not preempt  whatever decision we may or may not  often  and there's a that you seem to be asking  if I may say so a slightly hypothetical  question no it's not it's never gonna  work isn't it look listen let's talk  football let's talk football right  you're a man's arson vanga my man was  Alex Ferguson even Louie vanghoul knife  do you think they go into the dressing  room and they say listen boys hi we're  gonna line up tonight what are we gonna  do tonight you disagree do you want to  play in gold do you want to play golf no  they don't forget always said he had to  make it clear there was one boss he was  the boss that was it  that's not your sort of way of doing  things though my way of doing things  because it's politics it's community its  people it's government is actually if I  may say so not the same as managing a  football it's always into a competition  if you want to be a winner  if you wanna be a winner guys I want to  win do you want to beat do you want to  be Prime Minister can you do you wanna  win the league come on please do you  want yes Labor's doing very well  groups laying for a pleasure awesome or  do you want to win of course I want to  win and of course labour wants to win  that's why people have joined this party  that's why this party's growing that's  why we are united honor desires for the  hopes of ordinary people in this country  that is what's so strong about this yes  there goes going to be some discussions  about some issues obviously every party  has to have discussions about some  issues and at the end of the day we'll  come to a conclusion yes the room for  people who have different views in this  party of course there are no one party  can have a monopoly of one single wisdom  with a mass membership but of course you  have to come to a conclusion and we will  mr. Corbyn you certainly are different  you are very very different it's  fascinating as a politician talking to  you and having an exchange with you with  that there is no Dyke and let me ask you  this this is my curiosity and I see you  today the way I normally recognize you  without a tie yesterday you were wearing  a tired conference delivering that  magnificent  each is it true someone lent you that  tie the tie came from a friend of mine  because some of my team didn't like the  color of the tie that I was suggesting  it was one of those rather odd  discussions we have I like to appear as  comfortably as I possibly can and I'm  happy like this but I was very happy I  hope I hope you will agree looking very  smart and tidy yesterday would you agree  with that I would agree with that I did  figure thank you I thought the red was  the right choice what color had you got  on before the red it was a different  shade of red X Oh different shade of red  okay well I thought it suited you I  don't think there's a huge political  debate here but there is no what tell  you there is because I do think image is  very important and although you were  preaching to the converted I think the  general populace if you bear with me on  this they want to know does he look like  a 